{
  "name": "Getting Your Trim Just Right: A Step-by-Step Guide",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Getting interior trim to look perfect involves more than just nailing wood to a wall; it's about precision and patience. First off, you'll want to clear the room completely to give yourself ample space to work. Once that's done, it's all about verifying your layout and angles with some test cuts. This is super important, especially if your walls or rooms aren’t perfectly square, which is often the case in older homes. After you’ve got your measurements down, you’ll make those accurate miter or coping cuts. This is where the magic happens, and a skilled hand really shines. After the pieces are cut, they get installed. It’s not just about getting them on the wall; it’s about ensuring a tight, seamless fit. Finally, and this is crucial for that polished look, you'll set any nails below the surface and fill those tiny holes and gaps with putty or caulk. This final step preps everything beautifully for paint or stain. This process ensures a professional finish that truly elevates your home's interior. For larger projects or when you're aiming for a super high-end finish, especially with custom profiles or stain-grade work, bringing in a pro like HH Remodeling LLC can save you a lot of headache and ensure a flawless result.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
